LINUX COMMAND LINE CHEAT SHEET

BASIC NAVIGATION

→ pwd = Show current directory
→ ls = List files and directories
→ ls -l = List with details
→ ls -a = Show hidden files
→ cd directory = Change directory
→ cd .. = Go to parent directory
→ cd ~ = Go to home directory
→ clear = Clear terminal

FILE & DIRECTORY MANAGEMENT

→ touch file = Create empty file
→ mkdir dir = Create directory
→ mkdir -p dir/subdir = Create nested directories
→ rm file = Delete file
→ rm -r dir = Delete directory
→ cp src dest = Copy file
→ cp -r src dest = Copy directory
→ mv src dest = Move or rename
→ stat file = Show file details

VIEWING & READING FILES

→ cat file = View file contents
→ less file = Scroll through file
→ more file = View page by page
→ head file = First 10 lines
→ tail file = Last 10 lines
→ tail -f file = Live log updates
→ wc file = Count words/lines/chars

PERMISSIONS & OWNERSHIP

→ chmod 755 file = Change permissions
→ chmod +x file = Make executable
→ chown user file = Change owner
→ chown user:group file = Change owner & group
→ whoami = Current user

SEARCH & FIND

→ find . -name file = Find file
→ grep "text" file = Search in file
→ grep -r "text" dir = Recursive search
→ which command = Locate command
→ locate file = Fast file search

PROCESS MANAGEMENT

→ ps = Show processes
→ ps aux = All processes
→ top = Live monitor
→ htop = Advanced monitor
→ kill PID = Kill process
→ kill -9 PID = Force kill
→ jobs = Background jobs
→ bg = Run in background
→ fg = Bring to foreground

NETWORKING COMMANDS

→ ip a = Show interfaces
→ ping host = Test connectivity
→ curl url = Fetch data
→ wget url = Download file
→ netstat -tulpn = Open ports
→ ss -tulpn = Modern netstat

DISK & SYSTEM INFO

→ df -h = Disk usage
→ du -sh dir = Folder size
→ free -h = Memory usage
→ uname -a = System info
→ uptime = System uptime
→ lsblk = List disks

PACKAGE MANAGEMENT (DEBIAN/UBUNTU)

→ sudo apt update = Update packages
→ sudo apt upgrade = Upgrade packages
→ sudo apt install pkg = Install package
→ sudo apt remove pkg = Remove package
→ apt search pkg = Search packages

COMPRESSION & ARCHIVES

→ tar -cvf file.tar dir = Create archive
→ tar -xvf file.tar = Extract archive
→ zip file.zip files = Create zip
→ unzip file.zip = Extract zip
→ gzip file = Compress file
→ gunzip file.gz = Decompress file

REDIRECTION & PIPES

→ command > file = Redirect output
→ command >> file = Append output
→ command < file = Input redirection
→ command1 | command2 = Pipe commands
→ tee file = Output to file + terminal

OTHER USEFUL COMMANDS

→ history = Command history
→ !! = Repeat last command
→ alias ll='ls -la' = Create alias
→ man command = Manual page
→ sudo command = Run as admin
→ exit = Exit terminal
